*Has the business returned anything else in the past year?* Under the Business return reversal schedule of Northgate Rewards and Northgate+ Memberships, a business that seldom returns merchandise receives relief on the reversal, counted over every return recorded on the member's Northgate orders on Northgate Store and Online Orders dated within the twelve whole calendar months before today (a return dated on a day from which fewer than twelve whole calendar months have passed by today):

1. when the return is the only such return, it adds **0.1** to the relief fraction;
2. when it is one of exactly two such returns, it adds **0.05**;
3. otherwise it adds nothing.

**Hypothetical illustration.** Returns counted in the window: one (the return being reversed) adds 0.1; two add 0.05; four add nothing.
